### Documentation conventions

The documents above are the set this cluster ships with. Anything you add
follows the same rules.

- **Declare the source of truth** in the first paragraph of any document whose
  subject is also described elsewhere, and link rather than restate. An
  enumeration that must stay exact — apps, exports, namespaces, version pins —
  names the file that generates it.
- **An app README** (`kubernetes/apps/<app>/README.md`) covers what lives in that
  folder. Role READMEs live with the roles, in the platform collection.
- **No table of contents.** The heading structure is the navigation; a hand-kept
  table of contents only adds a second thing to drift.
- **Cross-links in a document you add go in a `## Related documentation` section
  at the foot**, holding internal links only, with third-party reading in an
  `## External references` list below it. `docs/RUNBOOKS.md` keeps its own
  `## Where the platform is documented` for the upstream-repository table.
- **Wrap prose at about 100 columns.** Tables, code blocks and URLs are exempt.
- **Commands are repository-root-relative** unless the document says otherwise,
  because that is the form the `task` wrappers and CI present.
- **A document describes the current state only.** One that stops doing so is
  deleted, with any still-current fact moved to the document that owns it.
- Every relative `.md` link is checked in CI, so a rename that breaks a
  cross-link fails the pipeline.

